 =========================================================
CSS NOTE: object-fit & object-fit: cover
========================================================= 



## About object-fit:

object-fit is a CSS property that controls how an image or
video fits inside its container.

* Works only on <img> and <video>
* Does NOT work on <div>
* Requires fixed width and height
* Similar to background-size but for media elements
  



## Understanding object-fit: cover:

Think of cover as "zoom to fill".

* The image is enlarged until the container is fully covered
* Aspect ratio is preserved
* Extra parts are cropped

If container and image ratios differ, cropping will happen.


## Why Cropping Occurs:

Image and container usually have different aspect ratios.
To avoid empty space, the browser zooms the image.
Overflowing areas are hidden.


## Required Conditions:

* Must set BOTH width and height
* Applies only to <img> and <video>
  

img {
width: 300px;
height: 200px;
object-fit: cover;
}



## Default Crop Position:

The center of the image stays visible by default.


img {
object-position: center; /* 50% 50% */
}


## Controlling Visible Area:

Use object-position to decide which part is shown.

img {
object-fit: cover;
object-position: top; /* top | bottom | left | right | center */
}


## Key Takeaways:

* cover fills the entire container
* No stretching or distortion
* Cropping is expected behavior
* Best for cards, banners, thumbnails
  
